      "lesson": "Verified evaluator feedback:\n- Bounding, rounding, or normalization was incorrect for some level sets.\n- The mixed-radix code/index mapping was not a complete round trip.\n- Failing behavior categories: custom_epsilon, mixed_radix_indexing, saturation\nFailed candidate rationale (do not repeat):\nCandidate rationale: I need to implement the FSQ (Finite Scalar Quantization) methods as specified. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. `quantize(values, levels, eps=1e-3)` - Returns normalized FSQ codes\n2. `codes_to_index(codes, levels)` - Maps normalized code vector to mixed-radix index\n3. `index_to_codes(index, levels)` - Maps index back to normalized code vector\n\nKey requirements:\n- Bound inputs with epsilon margin and even-level offset\n- Round bounded values and normalize to [-1, 1]\n- First dimension is least-significant in mixed-radix\n- Support both odd and even level counts\n- Maintain proper code/index round trips\n\nLet me break down the implementation:\n1. For quantize: bound values, round, normalize\n2. For codes_to_index: convert mixed-radix representation\n3. For index_to_codes: convert back from mixed-radix\n\nThe bounding function: f(z) = floor(L/2) * tanh(z) where L is levels\nThe normalization: (rounded_value + floor(L/2)) / floor(L/2) - 1 to get [-1, 1]\n\nFor mixed-radix conversion, I need to process dimensions from least to most significant.",
